snippet.textDisplay:
@fafster6439 Glad that helped—and great question.

The long-term goal with robots like this isn’t really dancing… it’s real-world assistance. Companies are aiming for humanoid robots that can work in places already built for humans—factories, warehouses, hospitals, even homes—handling repetitive or risky tasks. One interesting angle is that a human-shaped robot can use the same tools, stairs, and equipment we already use, so you don’t have to redesign entire environments.

Right now we’re seeing early “showcase” abilities, but the big push over the next few years will be practical jobs and autonomy.

