snippet.textDisplay:
@muhammadbagus1803 I get what you’re implying, but that’s exactly the kind of mindset a lot of people worry about with advanced robotics.

The real goal isn’t to replace or dominate humans—it’s to handle repetitive, dangerous, or high-risk tasks so people can focus on creative, strategic, and human-centered work. Historically, automation has shifted labor, not erased humanity.

The bigger conversation is about how we design and regulate this tech so it empowers people instead of exploiting anyone.

