snippet.textDisplay:
@janethcarpio9573 Great point — that natural, “feminine” gait is way harder than most people realize, especially the hip-to-shoulder timing. Dancing takes it to another level. Ballet-style moves are brutal for robots because it’s not just balance, it’s micro-adjustments + rhythm happening at the same time.

What’s interesting is that rhythm-based lifting (like relevés or small hops) is often where humanoids expose whether they’re relying on pre-scripted motion or real-time feedback control. That’s where things get really telling 👀

If XPENG pushed this into dance, would you rather see precise, technical ballet… or something more fluid like contemporary where timing can flex a bit? I’m actually digging into movement tests next, so curious what you’d want to see challenged first.

snippet.textOriginal:
